mber of permutations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $24$ tomes to choose from, so $n=24.$ We want to select $3$ of those tomes for Erik to read, so we have $r=3.$\n\nTherefore, the number of choices Erik has is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{24}{P}_{3} & =\\frac{24!}{(24-3)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{24!}{21!} \\\\  & =\\frac{24\\cdot 23\\cdot 22\\cdot \\cancel{21!}}{\\cancel{21!}} \\\\  & =24\\cdot 23\\cdot 22 \\\\  & =12\\,144.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-122479/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "256d3a08-0ade-51e9-887b-67250d5fae21"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122479"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
